Description: WebDAV server with SMB backend and NTLM authentication
 edulution-fileproxy exposes the shares of a Samba/Active Directory file server
 over WebDAV, so that desktop clients and the edulution web UI reach the same
 files through a single HTTPS endpoint. Callers authenticate against the domain
 controller, and every request is served over an SMB session belonging to that
 caller, which leaves the file server's own ACLs as the authority on what a user
 may read or write.
 .
 The package also installs edulution-fileproxy-reindex, an offline CLI that
 rebuilds the Elasticsearch index behind the wiki search endpoints, and the
 compose file for the Elasticsearch sidecar that the indexer expects on
 localhost. The wiki indexer is enabled in the shipped example configuration
 and needs the bring-up described in
 /usr/share/doc/edulution-fileproxy/README.Debian; the service is therefore
 installed neither enabled nor started.

